{"id":"route-decision","label":"Figure 6","title":"From where a firm stands to the routes that fit","kind":"pathway","synthesis":"conceptual","refs":[1,3,5,128,129,225,271,300,303,331,338,339,349,357,368,374,384,418,438,439,440,442,451,477,608,692,704,730,761,770,773,785,787,992,1028,1029,1031,1033,1040,1119],"data":"figures/data/route-decision.json","script":"figures/scripts/route-decision.py","caption":"A decision flow built from the situation tags on the route and program records. A firm starts from one of five situations; each leads to the route families that hold at least one route tagged for it, and each family opens onto its main routes with the text that governs them. A firm that is not yet registered meets the SAM.gov gate first, because registration is required when submitting an offer and at award [303](#cite:303). Set-asides and the certified programs rest on FAR Part 19 and 15 U.S.C. 644 [384](#cite:384) [374](#cite:374) [338](#cite:338) [349](#cite:349) [368](#cite:368) [357](#cite:357). SBIR and STTR rest on 15 U.S.C. 638, the SBA Policy Directive and Pub. L. 119-83 [3](#cite:3) [5](#cite:5) [1](#cite:1). Other transactions and commercial solutions openings rest on 10 U.S.C. 4021, 4022 and 3458 [1031](#cite:1031) [1028](#cite:1028) [1033](#cite:1033). Partnering routes rest on FAR subpart 9.6, 13 CFR Parts 121 and 125, and 10 U.S.C. 4902 [761](#cite:761) [770](#cite:770) [773](#cite:773) [785](#cite:785) [451](#cite:451). This is a conceptual figure: it shows which routes the records tag for each situation, not which routes any one firm qualifies for.","how_to_read":"Start at the left with the situation closest to yours and follow its lines to the route families; a thicker line means more of the routes shown carry that situation tag. Each family box fans out to its main routes on the right. A route box names the record to open, and the record names the governing text. If you are not yet registered, the gate box above that situation comes before any route.","explain":[{"on":"nodes: situation","text":"The five starting points the pathfinder asks about: not yet registered, registered with no award, first awards and growing, holding a technology that needs funding, and looking for partners. They are the situations tags on the records."},{"on":"nodes: family","text":"The four families of routes the guide is organised by: set-asides and vehicles, SBIR/STTR and innovation front doors, other transactions and commercial solutions openings, and primes and partnering."},{"on":"edges: situation to family","text":"Drawn where at least one of the routes shown is tagged for that situation in routes.yaml or programs.yaml. The routes list on each edge in the data file names them."},{"on":"node: SAM.gov gate","text":"An offeror is required to be registered in SAM when submitting an offer or quotation and at time of award; registration generates the Unique Entity ID [303](#cite:303) [608](#cite:608)."},{"on":"nodes: route","text":"One route or program record each, with its governing text. The 26 shown are the main routes of each family; the records hold the rest, including the agency programs and the individual consortia."}],"hotspots":[],"concepts":["how-a-buy-happens","what-a-set-aside-is","sbir-phases-101","other-transactions-101","partnering-forms-101"],"discussed_in":["1-why-this-matters","2-how-the-government-buys","9-how-to-read"],"source":"Conceptual figure drawn by the builder. Nodes and edges are in figures/data/route-decision.json; the situation and family of each route are taken from the situations and family fields of routes.yaml and programs.yaml as of October 3, 2026, and the governing texts from the governing_text field or the cited statute or regulation. No values were converted. Which 26 routes count as main is an editorial choice.","pathway":{"id":"route-decision","note":"Conceptual. Situation-to-family edges exist where at least one of the route nodes shown carries that situation tag in routes.yaml or programs.